                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Not Quite the Beginning - En-Gedi Resource Center](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110522-2762-0139-0000-aa2f1577925d:20)\n![Another Hebrew letter, letter bet. Knowledge is power!](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110522-2762-0139-0000-aa2f1577925d:21)\n![Hebrew Letter Bet: Exploring its Christian Significance](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110522-2762-0139-0000-aa2f1577925d:22)\n![Bet hebrew letter icon – Royalty-Free Vector | VectorStock](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110522-2762-0139-0000-aa2f1577925d:23)\n![Hebrew Letter Bet: Exploring its Christian Significance](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110522-2762-0139-0000-aa2f1577925d:24)\n\nThe [Bet (letter)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bet_(letter)) is the `second letter of the Hebrew alphabet` (ב) and carries a numerical value (gematria) of **2**.[[1]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bet_(letter))[[2]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137074/jewish/Bet-Vet.htm)\n\n### Key Details\n\n- **Meaning:** The name *Bet* (or *Bayit* ) means **\"house\"** or **\"tent\"**.[[1]](https://rosenhebrewschool.com/articles/the-letter-bet/)[[2]](https://halyministries.com/hebrew-letter-bet-exploring-its-christian-significance/)\n- **Pronunciation & Dagesh:** \n\t- With a dot inside (*dagesh* ), it is **Bet** , pronounced like the English **\"b\"**.\n\t- Without the dot, it becomes **Vet** , pronounced like **\"v\"** . This alternation is part of the *Begadkefat* letter group.[[1]](https://hebrewtoday.com/alphabet/the-hebrew-letter-bet/)[[2]](https://rosenhebrewschool.com/articles/the-letter-bet/)[[3]](https://www.quora.com/I-am-learning-Hebrew-and-I-am-very-confused-Can-someone-explain-the-aleph-bet-and-what-roles-the-letters-play)\n- **First Letter of the Torah:** The Hebrew Bible begins with Bet in the word *Bereshit* (\"In the beginning...\").[[1]](https://rosenhebrewschool.com/articles/the-letter-bet/)\n- **Symbolism:** It represents duality, creation, and a physical or spiritual \"house\" (such as the body housing the soul, or the world housing humanity).[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137074/jewish/Bet-Vet.htm)[[2]](https://gabrielelevy.com/pages/the-letter-bet)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=12Mgsjsc6bY)\n\nWould you like to know more about its **gematria**, **mystical meanings in Judaism** , or **how to write it**?",
